{{ end }}- Keep issue context current as you work:
  - Keep notes terse and evidence-oriented: final commands run, key outputs/assertions, files changed, AC pass/fail, blockers, and remaining scope only.
  - Do not append raw logs, exploratory transcripts, routine progress narration, duplicate primer context, or speculative scratch work to notes.
  - Update the active issue's design/notes as decisions change; capture subtask-level detail on the relevant child issue instead of bloating a parent/epic description.
  - `az issue get` hides historical notes in text output by default; use `az issue get <issue-id> --with-notes` only when full note history is needed.
  - Use status/priority/labels flags when state changes materially.
  - Status update rule: move your active issue to `in_progress` when starting; use `in_review` only when the requested work is complete but awaiting review/integration; use `closed` only when acceptance criteria are met and required integration/validation is done.
- Overlay edits: check `az spec read --issue <issue-id>` before behavior changes, keep `View()` and `Size()` aligned, validate default and narrow viewports, and update goldens when rendered output changes. If the work is docs/process-only, record `Spec impact: none (docs/process-only)` in issue notes.
